From 9f313659f546a139f07aaf5ea0f485aa6c622892 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Blot <emmanuel.blot@free.fr>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 18:18:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hw/arm: yosemite5: add Facebook Yosemite 5 BMC
 machine

Add an AST2600-based machine for the Facebook Yosemite 5 platform,
modelled from its device tree (aspeed-bmc-facebook-yosemite5.dts).

The board uses TMP75, LM75B and TMP421 temperature sensors, INA230 and
INA238 power monitors, ADC128D818 ADCs, PCA9535 and PCA9536 IO
expanders, PCA9546 I2C muxes, AT24C EEPROMs and a DS1339 RTC, including
the CXL board reachable through a nested mux pair.

Every device the Yosemite 5 device tree describes and QEMU already
models is instantiated. The remaining ones (XDP710, LTC4287, MP5998,
TPS25990, ISL28022 and INA233 power monitors, the RAA228006 PSU
controller, ADS7830 ADCs, MAX31790 fan controllers, the TMP432
temperature sensor, the SBRMI and SBTSI side-band interfaces and MCTP)
have no QEMU model and are left documented as comments.

Signed-off-by: Emmanuel Blot <emmanuel.blot@free.fr>
---
 docs/system/arm/aspeed.rst        |   1 +
 hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600_yosemite5.c | 218 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 hw/arm/meson.build                |   1 +
 3 files changed, 220 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600_yosemite5.c

